WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:12.120
Exciting frontiers in quorum sensing is to actually figure out, 

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.470
how does this work,

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.390
not in a flask in a laboratory?

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.250
So how is quorum sensing playing out 

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.970
in biology, in life?

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.780
So I think one area of particular high interest right 

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.150
now is the microbiome.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:35.680
So what's also been learned in the past twenty or so years, 

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:40.710
is that every higher organism lives in a fantastic 

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.790
community with bacteria.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:43.440
So,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.180
for example,

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.210
in the human gut,

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:50.180
there are 10^14 bacteria in there, 600 different species,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.980
and they are giving us life.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.030
And they're doing all these processes, and helping us digest our food, and educate our immune system, and 

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.930
make all kinds of micronutrients.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.550
And so these bacteria that are living in our gut,

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.350
for example,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:07.200
are keeping us alive. Quorum sensing has to be happening in there.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.630
And so what I wonder,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.310
is 10^14 bacteria, 600 species,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.600
all using their own blends of molecules,

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.510
plus there's curves and flow, and my human genetics, and what I eat,

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.390
and when I ate it, and there's space, and there's time, and how in the 

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:29.230
world can quorum sensing be kept straight? Like, how are these bacteria 

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.590
not getting confused?

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:30.800
You know,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.220
how do they actually do the correct jobs in time, in space,

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:40.360
in the face of bacteria that they're cooperating with and 

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.010
bacteria that they're enemies with?

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.850
And somehow, here I am, they're doing it. And so 

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.140
I would just love--

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:52.840
and I think there's a big effort to try-- to understand how does quorum sensing happen in 

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.700
mixed species, in real time,

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.010
when conditions are not ideal,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.000
like in a flask in a lab?

00:02:00.565 --> 00:02:05.365
And I think figuring that out is a really hard and wonderful 

00:02:05.755 --> 00:02:06.225
problem,

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:11.095
and I think that's what scientists are going to have their eyeballs on going into these next 

00:02:11.095 --> 00:02:11.855
ten years.

